/*
 * Declares the EnumFieldAccessValue class.
 *
 * EnumFieldAccessValue represents a compile-time field access on an enumeration
 * type. Unlike ordinary field accesses, this operator does not read from a
 * runtime object. Instead, it resolves an enum member directly from the enum
 * type itself. The accessed value is stored inside this operator, and the
 * `object` inherited from FieldOperatorValue is always `UNIT_VALUE`.
 *
 * This operator is used when referencing an enum member such as:
 *
 *     MyEnum::Variant
 *
 * The access is resolved statically, and the resulting value is embedded in the
 * operator. Enum field accesses never produce lvalues.


 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::fields::enum_
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/fields/enum_.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-03-02
